# Buy Product Checkout Flow Implementation Plan

This document outlines the architecture and execution plan for the AgriChain Buy Product (Checkout) module. The flow involves selecting quantity, defining delivery details, reviewing pricing, confirming the order, deducting stock securely, and recording mock blockchain verifications.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Mock Features vs Actual Flow:** 
> - The **Wallet Payment Processing** and **Arbitrum Smart Contract Execution** will be implemented as robust mock simulations in the backend. 
> - **Coupons** will be mock-validated (e.g. `DISCOUNT50` gives ₹50 off) for UI demonstration.
> - **Addresses** will be temporarily handled in component state or local storage for speed, unless you want them persisted to the `User` MongoDB document.

## Open Questions
- Do you want the delivery addresses to be saved persistently into the `User` document in MongoDB, or just handled locally for this checkout session demo?
- For the success screen, do you want the "Download Invoice" button to actually generate a PDF, or just show a "Coming Soon" toast for now?

